<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids rebound on MGE rise.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids rebound on MGE rise.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash bids for dark northern spring wheat rebounded on Tuesday, buoyed by gains in MGE futures, and movement picked up slightly as demand from the Pacific Northwest increased, cash dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We're seeing a little more interest out there,&quot; a Montana dealer said. &quot;Most of the offers are to the PNW on train.&quot;</p>
<p>Crop conditions continued to be of concern to farmers in eastern Montana and North Dakota where a dry June left some fields badly damaged, dealers said. In the Red River Valley, excess rainfall was blamed for crop damage. USDA on Monday confirmed condition ratings had deteriorated.  </p>
